RODNEY:
Over the next seven weeks,

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:22.889
I'll be joined by actors,
directors and key collaborators,

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:25.258
to break down each episode
of season two.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:28.261
JERRY BUSS:
<i>It's not about basketball.
 It's about winning.</i>

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.329
RODNEY: We'll also unpack
the real events

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:33.900
that make it into the show
with sportswriter Jeff Pearlman.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.769
His book about
the Showtime Lakers of the 1980s

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.004
inspired<i> Winning Time.</i>

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.739
 JEFF PEARLMAN:<i> So after
 the Lakers win this game</i>

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:40.807
<i>that they shouldn't have won,</i>

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.608
<i>on a court they shouldn't
 have won on,</i>

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:43.810
<i> the fans went crazy,</i>

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:46.412
<i> and all of these things
 actually happened.</i>

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.549
RODNEY: Listen to HBO's official
<i> Winning Time Podcast</i>

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.050
